						 <blockquote> <p><strong>Author:</strong> <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/torrential" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1888201&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1540360055" alt="Torrential" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1888201)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/torrential" >Torrential</a></span><br /> <strong>Translator:</strong> <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-benji" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1575709&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1540360055" alt="Dr Benji" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1575709)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-benji" >Dr Benji</a></span><br /> <strong>Date of creation:</strong> 2014-09-26<br /> <strong>Original:</strong> <a href="http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/scp-054-fr">SCP-054-FR</a> in the French branch<br /> <strong>Translation:</strong> <a href="http://scp-int.wikidot.com/scp-054-fr">SCP-054-FR</a> in the Translation Archive<br /> <strong>Image:</strong> Montage by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drgemini" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2184104&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1540360055" alt="DrGemini" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2184104)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drgemini" >DrGemini</a></span>, CC BY-SA</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>Additional Context:</strong><br /> French SCPs use a threat level in addition to the normal classification, which is indicated with a color code. You can find an overview of the color codes <a href="http://scp-int.wikidot.com/niveaux-de-menace-des-objets-scp">here</a>.</p> <p>Color code Orange means:<br /> <em>The object is unpredictable, exhibiting dangerous properties and is difficult to recontain. It is generally the lowest level assigned to humanoid entities. Often assigned to Euclid and Keter class objects.</em></p> 
